      "explanation": "The setupLeaderState declaration and lines 455–464 support the stored anchor and behavior description. Each invocation creates fresh commitCh and stepDown channels and a fresh commitment object. startStopReplication copies the commitment pointer and stepDown channel into new replication instances. The new consumer evidence shows leaderLoop selecting the current leaderState.commitCh and reading the current leaderState.commitment. updateLastAppended reports through the retained instance pointer, and commitment.recalculate notifies that object's channel. This supports isolation of these particular reporting paths across separately constructed leader states. It does not establish complete isolation of all late work. Issues d5b4659386c74250b78fb47e45c35dc7 and 9267ec89b45d4429b9df543fbc373522 remain open because accessor semantics, configuration legality and the selected unit's actual code_uses remain unavailable.",
      "alternatives": "Fresh object and channel identities can isolate late match reports without requiring workers to terminate before the next leader lifetime. This mechanism does not validate the reports themselves or the constructor arguments.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "A correctly isolated commitment object could still receive an inaccurate retained-history report or be initialized with an unjustified threshold or configuration. Consequently, the construction mapping cannot establish O_append_support or rule out the goal's bad outcome.",
