      "explanation": "The runLeader declaration anchors the narrower behavior range containing setup, deferred cleanup, replication startup, no-op dispatch and leaderLoop invocation. Cleanup closes stop channels and clears references without a visible worker join. The new range shows leaderLoop consuming current leader-owned channels and reading the current commitment object; retained worker pointers therefore support isolation of late match notifications from a subsequent freshly constructed object. This is narrower than complete late-completion isolation or transport shutdown. The range ends within the commit branch before its remaining handling is visible. dispatchLogs also explicitly permits persistence failure and transition to Follower, so no-op dispatch is not a commitment guarantee. Issues 59b03633f62943a18e86039aaaf650c5 and a19c3efb6b9941428c5d4cf10e2997dd remain open.",
