      "explanation": "The boundary direction from O_append_support to B_setup_leader_state appropriately identifies a producer of the context in which support is credited. The handoff is explicit: setupLeaderState creates the object, startStopReplication retains its pointer, and successful nonempty requests reach updateLastAppended and commitment.match. The new evidence extends this chain through notification to leaderLoop's read of its current commitment object. commitment.match's documented disk-agreement precondition and docs/apply.md's persistence-before-application expectation explain why this boundary matters. They do not establish valid membership, threshold inputs or truthful acknowledgments. The lifetime-consumption component is partially answered, but the compound conditions of issues 080aa260cf4645e497c9b2b9567a8b10 and dadb9275ccce4c598929bd66427f0c05 remain unresolved.",
